The Associated Press issued a correction Friday after it filed a misleading alert about a judge's ruling in a gay-marriage case. "The AP initially misunderstood the scope of the judge��s statement," the news coop tells Poynter in an email.
The AP has issued a correction:
CORRECTION: Judge says he will order Ohio to recognize out-of-state gay marriages. (Previously said judge would strike down Ohio ban.) — The Associated Press (@AP) April 4, 2014
Earlier, BuzzFeed legal editor Chris Geidner called out AP after the alert went out:
BREAKING: Federal judge says he will issue ruling that will strike down Ohio's ban on gay marriage. — The Associated Press (@AP) April 4, 2014
The @AP is AGAIN wrong about a marriage case decision. More to come... — Chris Geidner (@chrisgeidner) April 4, 2014
The Ohio case at issue is a marriage recognition case, not a full marriage equality case, so there will not be a full marriage ruling. — Chris Geidner (@chrisgeidner) April 4, 2014
For those confused by the @AP, here's my report on Ohio & marriage: http://t.co/aXgNzaaOPV — Chris Geidner (@chrisgeidner) April 4, 2014
